WEBVTT

00:00:02.109 --> 00:00:05.279
Once, when many planets
intermingled and

00:00:05.613 --> 00:00:08.716
the boundary between man
and god was vague...

00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:14.221
There was a tale of a particular family.
A tale of love and rebirth.

00:00:17.892 --> 00:00:27.167
Sometimes I think things over.
It helps to cheer me up.

00:00:34.942 --> 00:00:37.678
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:44.552
This place has always
meant everything to me.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:49.823
It rains so beautifully here.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:55.296
I can dance like the wind.

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:00.801
Even now, I'm having fun.

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:06.640
I have a better sense of
rhythm than you'd think.

00:01:07.141 --> 00:01:12.313
It felt as though every time
I heard a certain someone's voice,

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:22.723
I would think back to how
I grew up surrounded by laughter.

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:28.796
Yes, anywhere would have
done as a place to call home.

00:01:28.796 --> 00:01:34.301
Farewell, sunshine!
The night rises up invitingly.

00:01:34.501 --> 00:01:39.573
It's okay, this world moves
in a way that will connect us.

00:01:39.807 --> 00:01:46.280
So that we can all smile
together once again.

00:01:54.421 --> 00:01:55.255
Don't cry.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:01:58.058
They're gone.

00:01:59.793 --> 00:02:02.029
We have to make the best
of things on our own.

00:02:03.631 --> 00:02:04.932
We'll make our own rules.

00:02:05.866 --> 00:02:09.003
The three of us should
always decide how to deal

00:02:09.703 --> 00:02:11.805
with problems and new things together.

00:02:15.943 --> 00:02:17.044
It'll be fine.

00:02:21.115 --> 00:02:25.586
The Eldest and His
Happy Science Team

00:02:26.787 --> 00:02:28.956
It's not fair that you get her all the time!

00:02:29.256 --> 00:02:31.325
| want Koto, too!

00:02:31.558 --> 00:02:34.595
I'm not letting her stay at
my place 'cause I want to!

00:02:35.195 --> 00:02:38.599
Thanks to them,
I'm not getting any sleep!

00:02:40.801 --> 00:02:42.936
You didn't try anything
with Koto because

00:02:42.936 --> 00:02:45.439
you can't spend the nights
at some woman's place—

00:02:45.439 --> 00:02:46.774
Hell no!

00:02:46.774 --> 00:02:48.909
If I wanted something as
flat as a cutting board,

00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:50.778
I've got one in my kitchen already!

00:02:50.778 --> 00:02:52.746
Then why not let me have her?

00:02:52.746 --> 00:02:53.981
Fine, take her!

00:02:53.981 --> 00:02:55.949
She's a glutton and
has nothing upstairs,

00:02:55.949 --> 00:02:58.552
<i>SO make sure your
monsters don't eat her!</i>

00:02:58.819 --> 00:02:59.753
That's enough.

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:05.325
We already decided what
we would do with her.

00:03:06.026 --> 00:03:09.096
And you both gave your assent to it.

00:03:11.398 --> 00:03:12.132
But...

00:03:12.132 --> 00:03:13.167
But!

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.369
No buts.

00:03:15.636 --> 00:03:18.238
Our meeting for today is finished.

00:03:21.208 --> 00:03:24.044
In our name, and in the
name of our great mother!

00:03:24.545 --> 00:03:26.914
We will obey the
Ten Bloodless Commandments.

00:03:30.951 --> 00:03:33.220
You're always like that.

00:03:34.354 --> 00:03:36.924
The Council of Three is just for show.

00:03:37.558 --> 00:03:39.226
You decide everything on your own.

00:03:39.793 --> 00:03:42.162
We don't have any choice.

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:48.635
| always try to make
the best choice for us.

00:03:48.869 --> 00:03:54.575
Taking away my doll wasn't the best
choice for me, it was the worst.

00:03:57.111 --> 00:04:00.080
There's no need to fight

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.350
Chapter 7: The Present (38)/
Kurama Temple A over the girl.

00:04:03.584 --> 00:04:05.185
Hey, there!

00:04:05.652 --> 00:04:06.553
We're here.

00:04:07.154 --> 00:04:08.922
Is this the bad guys' lair?

00:04:08.922 --> 00:04:10.190
We're coming in!

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:11.558
Who are you calling bad guys?

00:04:11.992 --> 00:04:12.993
See?

00:04:15.129 --> 00:04:16.663
High tech!

00:04:16.864 --> 00:04:17.898
| didn't expect this.

00:04:18.799 --> 00:04:21.168
This is the heart of
the Looking Glass City.

00:04:21.168 --> 00:04:23.137
It controls every system in the city.

00:04:24.271 --> 00:04:26.373
- You in the sailor outfit, especially!
- Huh?

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:30.277
You'd better not swing your
weapon around in here!

00:04:31.678 --> 00:04:32.212
This?

00:04:34.581 --> 00:04:35.916
Put that away!

00:04:35.916 --> 00:04:37.251
I'm W a r n in 9 Yy o u !

00:04:37.985 --> 00:04:39.419
Interesting...

00:04:39.653 --> 00:04:40.721
Sis!

00:04:47.728 --> 00:04:49.863
What did I just say?!

00:04:49.863 --> 00:04:51.131
What is this place?

00:04:51.532 --> 00:04:55.402
- This is really well-made.
- No! Don't take it out of the box!

00:04:55.402 --> 00:04:57.638
Oh, fine.

00:04:58.305 --> 00:04:59.039
A! Un!

00:05:05.612 --> 00:05:07.147
Don't stop me, Fushimi!

00:05:07.147 --> 00:05:09.516
She's done something unforgivable!

00:05:10.384 --> 00:05:11.485
Now, now...

00:05:12.119 --> 00:05:14.955
She destroyed my dreams with her magical item!

00:05:14.955 --> 00:05:17.691
Magical Girl
A Magical Girl must never do that!

00:05:17.858 --> 00:05:18.826
It's unforgivable!

00:05:18.992 --> 00:05:20.360
That's what upset you?

00:05:20.994 --> 00:05:22.396
It's not magic.

00:05:22.796 --> 00:05:24.865
It was made in the Shrine's lab.

00:05:30.737 --> 00:05:31.805
You want to borrow it?

00:05:31.805 --> 00:05:32.840
What? Really?

00:05:33.173 --> 00:05:34.675
If you promise to give it back.

00:05:34.908 --> 00:05:37.377
Maybe you're not so bad after all!

00:05:38.645 --> 00:05:41.381
Okay, Fushimi, you finish
showing her around!

00:05:41.381 --> 00:05:41.982
A! Un!

00:05:41.982 --> 00:05:43.217
Roger!

00:05:44.284 --> 00:05:48.488
| didn't bring anything with me that
had obvious, exploitable weak spots.

00:05:48.956 --> 00:05:51.391
I'm sorry you seem to
have misunderstood,

00:05:51.859 --> 00:05:54.795
but the only thing driving
my boss is simple curiosity.

00:05:56.363 --> 00:05:58.498
Shouko-chan's cute, isn't she?

00:05:59.299 --> 00:06:01.435
They're just there for...
well, just in case.

00:06:01.902 --> 00:06:03.937
Aratama"s a little special.

00:06:03.937 --> 00:06:06.173
It's not like she'll be able
to do anything with it.

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:10.010
Anyway, this place kind of
reminds me of the Shrine's labs.

00:06:10.978 --> 00:06:13.881
Build a place to meet
a set of requirements,

00:06:14.381 --> 00:06:17.150
and it'll wind up looking the
same just about everywhere.

00:06:17.885 --> 00:06:20.020
Let's go. The monk awaits.

00:06:20.787 --> 00:06:21.555
Kurama-san.

00:06:21.955 --> 00:06:22.456
Yes.

00:06:22.789 --> 00:06:25.459
The man in charge here
at Kurama Temple,

00:06:25.792 --> 00:06:27.794
and the leader of the Council of Three.

00:06:28.362 --> 00:06:30.931
The de-facto ruler of the town.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.368
You're not all that alike.

00:06:35.435 --> 00:06:36.603
The Council of Three.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.572
True, I suppose.

00:06:39.106 --> 00:06:43.610
Yase isn't really human,
and neither am I.

00:06:44.244 --> 00:06:45.245
Really...

00:06:45.512 --> 00:06:48.548
Myoue's the one most like you.

00:06:49.516 --> 00:06:50.651
...human?

00:06:51.551 --> 00:06:53.387
It's rather complicated.

00:06:54.521 --> 00:06:56.323
A long story.

00:06:59.393 --> 00:07:01.495
It seems like people really rely on you,

00:07:01.495 --> 00:07:03.730
so I suppose it doesn't
matter too much, does it?

00:07:03.997 --> 00:07:05.065
| suppose not.

00:07:05.432 --> 00:07:06.967
Whatever works, works.

00:07:07.968 --> 00:07:09.036
That's right.

00:07:10.470 --> 00:07:12.572
You may have already heard this,

00:07:13.206 --> 00:07:16.643
but we rule this city in
place of our parents.

00:07:17.978 --> 00:07:21.114
We've done so for a very long time,

00:07:22.316 --> 00:07:24.952
but we've never had a guest like you.

00:07:25.419 --> 00:07:28.655
I've never been to a place
like this, either.

00:07:29.423 --> 00:07:32.125
| think my teacher knew about it,
but nobody else did.

00:07:34.962 --> 00:07:39.900
I'd like to meet this
teacher of yours someday.

00:07:40.167 --> 00:07:41.335
He's pretty weird.

00:07:42.069 --> 00:07:44.004
But maybe you'll have
the chance someday.

00:07:44.504 --> 00:07:49.443
We have no real means of contact
with the outside world.

00:07:49.810 --> 00:07:51.945
That's just a fact of this place.

00:07:54.514 --> 00:07:56.817
| wish to leave this world.

00:07:57.551 --> 00:08:00.420
That's been the one thought on
my mind since I was a child.

00:08:02.255 --> 00:08:04.691
You must want to go home, too, I'm sure.

00:08:05.158 --> 00:08:07.794
If there's anything I can do, tell me.

00:08:08.228 --> 00:08:09.863
Thank you.

00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:12.499
If there's anything I can help with, too...

00:08:12.499 --> 00:08:13.934
I'll remember that.

00:08:16.703 --> 00:08:19.906
So, tell me, have you found any
clues as to what you're looking for?

00:08:20.273 --> 00:08:21.975
Still looking!

00:08:22.743 --> 00:08:27.347
The words "black rabbit” do ring a bell...

00:08:28.115 --> 00:08:30.350
But unfortunately,
she's not here right now,

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:31.752
so I can't introduce you.

00:08:32.719 --> 00:08:36.590
Our mother is a black rabbit,
drawn by our father.

00:08:39.059 --> 00:08:42.062
Just one of those coincidences
that happen all the time.

00:08:42.062 --> 00:08:44.064
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:08:44.064 --> 00:08:45.532
Chapter 8: The Past (6)/ Kurama

00:08:49.569 --> 00:08:50.570
What is this?

00:08:51.038 --> 00:08:52.039
| made them.

00:08:52.406 --> 00:08:54.374
From now on you three are siblings.

00:08:54.608 --> 00:08:56.576
It'll be so much more
lively from now on!

00:08:56.576 --> 00:08:57.944
You made them?

00:08:58.378 --> 00:09:00.414
I'm your older brother.

00:09:03.316 --> 00:09:04.751
I'm your older sister!

00:09:08.622 --> 00:09:09.823
No way!

00:09:09.823 --> 00:09:11.091
You're a demon!

00:09:11.324 --> 00:09:12.592
Does it really matter?

00:09:14.628 --> 00:09:16.463
- Oh, no!
- I see you're getting along already!

00:09:20.767 --> 00:09:23.437
None is like the Buddha,

00:09:23.970 --> 00:09:26.440
and if you seek one like him,
they shall not be found.

00:09:26.706 --> 00:09:32.079
Without an understanding of
the law, one cannot truly see.

00:09:32.512 --> 00:09:36.783
The Buddha and his powers are
beyond what words can express,

00:09:37.084 --> 00:09:40.353
and he stays with us forever,
never leaving nor coming,

00:09:40.687 --> 00:09:42.789
sharing the law with the masses.

00:09:46.026 --> 00:09:46.827
Bathroom.

00:09:48.862 --> 00:09:50.263
It's okay, Yase!

00:09:50.263 --> 00:09:51.765
We'll find it together!

00:09:53.767 --> 00:09:55.235
Where did you lose it?

00:09:59.506 --> 00:10:00.273
This?

00:10:02.476 --> 00:10:04.077
| found you!

00:10:05.112 --> 00:10:07.981
It got stuck when you were
crawling under the shrine.

00:10:07.981 --> 00:10:09.182
Thanks, Kuruma!

00:10:09.649 --> 00:10:11.084
But how did you know?

00:10:11.852 --> 00:10:14.354
| just looked at all the mud on her...

00:10:17.257 --> 00:10:18.859
You're that far already?

00:10:22.596 --> 00:10:24.798
| want to go to the capital to play.

00:10:26.967 --> 00:10:28.335
What's it like?

00:10:29.569 --> 00:10:30.403
The capital.

00:10:31.905 --> 00:10:33.874
There're shrines and temples,

00:10:33.874 --> 00:10:35.041
and houses,

00:10:35.041 --> 00:10:36.510
and lots of people.

00:10:36.943 --> 00:10:39.146
And sometimes there's a market.

00:10:39.613 --> 00:10:40.514
It's fun.

00:10:43.884 --> 00:10:45.285
Want to sneak out and go?

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:47.354
No.

00:10:47.787 --> 00:10:49.256
Dad said I couldn't.

00:10:50.557 --> 00:10:51.858
Bored.

00:10:55.128 --> 00:10:56.096
Can I have this?

00:10:56.596 --> 00:10:57.364
Fine.

00:10:57.631 --> 00:10:58.999
Let's play kemari.

00:11:04.905 --> 00:11:05.539
Hey...

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.808
| want to go to the capital.

00:11:09.442 --> 00:11:10.110
No.

00:11:11.378 --> 00:11:12.045
Why?

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:13.513
| told you.

00:11:13.713 --> 00:11:15.749
That's the human world.

00:11:17.817 --> 00:11:21.054
Don't you think I look like a human?

00:11:21.421 --> 00:11:23.690
You only look like one, that's all.

00:11:27.127 --> 00:11:29.963
That's where the government is, too.

00:11:30.797 --> 00:11:33.099
If they found you,
you'd be in big trouble.

00:11:34.801 --> 00:11:36.102
Let's play ball.

00:11:36.102 --> 00:11:39.973
No. I'm not as dumb
or as strong as you.

00:11:41.107 --> 00:11:42.676
I'm the elder,

00:11:42.909 --> 00:11:44.044
and the smarter,

00:11:44.044 --> 00:11:45.178
and the more elegant...

00:11:45.412 --> 00:11:46.746
And shorter.

00:11:46.746 --> 00:11:47.981
And nicer.

00:11:49.182 --> 00:11:50.984
But I'm jealous of you.

00:11:54.854 --> 00:11:59.459
You've got a human body, and you
know the world outside this place.

00:12:00.927 --> 00:12:03.663
The capital's not that special.
You'll be able to go someday.

00:12:05.398 --> 00:12:12.739
Kousanji Family Timeline: Priest Myoue moves to the mountains. Koto falls in love with him. The priest slacks off. An exasperated Buddhalocanii lends Koto her body. The priest starts to live with Koto. Some
more stuff happens. Yakushimaru comes. Some more stuff happens. Kurama and Yase come. Some more stuff happens. The Shrine finds out about them. The priest gets mad at Kurama. They move to the Looking Glass City.

00:12:42.035 --> 00:12:45.171
From now on, you can go down to
the capital whenever you like!

00:12:49.542 --> 00:12:51.111
The Looking Glass City

00:12:56.483 --> 00:12:58.184
| liked the mountain better!

00:12:58.418 --> 00:13:00.287
Nobody asked you to come.

00:13:15.635 --> 00:13:17.570
Did I make it just like you wanted?

00:13:19.739 --> 00:13:22.676
If there's anything else
you need, tell me.

00:13:23.677 --> 00:13:26.279
| know there's a lot
you've had to do without.

00:13:27.147 --> 00:13:28.982
Thanks, Dad!

00:13:32.986 --> 00:13:34.521
That's amazing!

00:13:38.024 --> 00:13:40.393
Wow! I don't know
what it is, but wow!

00:13:44.164 --> 00:13:46.599
- What is that thing?
- That's the most awesome one yet!

00:13:48.968 --> 00:13:50.837
You're amazing.

00:13:52.205 --> 00:13:53.673
It's strange for me to say,

00:13:54.007 --> 00:13:56.242
but I'm proud to have
such a talented son.

00:13:58.044 --> 00:14:00.880
Kurama. What will you do in the future?

00:14:01.848 --> 00:14:07.187
Someday... I think I'd like
to see the outside world.

00:14:07.887 --> 00:14:11.758
| want to find out what I'm really worth,
some place that isn't here.

00:14:12.592 --> 00:14:13.727
I'll help you.

00:14:55.034 --> 00:14:57.036
Ky OuUSsS O UGI G A

00:14:57.036 --> 00:14:58.505
Chapter 9: The Present
(4)/ Kurama Temple B

00:15:04.711 --> 00:15:08.515
Adamantine Giant Bishamaru
Adamantine Giant Bishamaru!

00:15:10.550 --> 00:15:23.763
The shadow of evil threatens
beautiful Looking Glass City!

00:15:23.763 --> 00:15:25.532
Take this! Buddha Punch!

00:15:25.532 --> 00:15:27.300
Evil-bashing Kick!

00:15:27.300 --> 00:15:34.507
And don't forget
the controller of justice!

00:15:34.841 --> 00:15:37.677
Controller—

00:15:38.445 --> 00:15:41.114
It's not here. It's not here.
It's not here.

00:15:41.381 --> 00:15:44.017
It's not here! It's not here!
It's not here!

00:15:44.017 --> 00:15:45.485
It's not here!

00:15:45.852 --> 00:15:47.287
What's not here?

00:15:47.787 --> 00:15:48.154
Ow!

00:15:49.489 --> 00:15:51.257
My controller! What else?!

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.061
Out of Order

00:15:56.996 --> 00:15:58.932
Miyakoi!
How is your day, Shouko?

00:15:58.932 --> 00:16:00.633
Crappy. Get me the four gods.

00:16:01.100 --> 00:16:02.435
Looking for something again?

00:16:02.435 --> 00:16:05.705
The Four Gods Have Appeared! Seiryuu Aoi Byakko
Haku Suzaku Shushu Genbu Zakuro We'll start looking!

00:16:05.872 --> 00:16:07.140
Sure, thanks.

00:16:11.144 --> 00:16:12.912
- What's that?
- A replacement.

00:16:13.179 --> 00:16:15.148
Load the OS on it and it's
just as good, right?

00:16:15.515 --> 00:16:16.282
Idiot.

00:16:17.116 --> 00:16:20.353
| told you to put a GPS on it!

00:16:20.353 --> 00:16:22.722
Why would 1?
It's not like I'd misplace it!

00:16:26.125 --> 00:16:29.128
It was here just yesterday afternoon.

00:16:29.596 --> 00:16:31.598
Yesterday afternoon...

00:16:32.298 --> 00:16:32.799
Ah!

00:16:38.137 --> 00:16:40.340
Let's eat!

00:16:43.776 --> 00:16:45.345
Yum!

00:16:45.345 --> 00:16:46.946
Don't talk with your mouth full.

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:47.881
Elbows!

00:16:48.114 --> 00:16:49.482
| want more broth!

00:16:49.682 --> 00:16:51.351
Get it yourself.

00:16:57.257 --> 00:16:58.191
A guest?

00:16:58.191 --> 00:17:00.159
Nobody's home!

00:17:13.172 --> 00:17:14.841
Get me the three stooges.

00:17:15.275 --> 00:17:16.643
It's Shouko-chan.

00:17:16.643 --> 00:17:17.377
The gamer.

00:17:17.877 --> 00:17:18.978
The otaku.

00:17:19.178 --> 00:17:19.712
Shaddap!

00:17:20.713 --> 00:17:22.682
Where's my controller?

00:17:23.716 --> 00:17:25.251
Don't try and play dumb!

00:17:25.251 --> 00:17:26.319
What's wrong?

00:17:26.553 --> 00:17:28.755
| have no idea what you're talking about.

00:17:28.755 --> 00:17:30.023
Did you bump your head?

00:17:30.823 --> 00:17:32.692
That stupid eldest son!

00:17:40.433 --> 00:17:44.771
If you want to play, do it outside!

00:17:49.008 --> 00:17:52.145
An emergency inspection by Kurama Temple

00:17:52.145 --> 00:17:53.780
Kurama again?
Is currently underway.

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:57.317
A Message from Kurama Temple: Inspection in progress up ahead. Thank you for your cooperation.
- What's going on today? - Thank you for your cooperation.

00:17:57.951 --> 00:17:59.319
Repeat.

00:17:59.552 --> 00:18:03.756
Checkpoint
1 Hour Only!

00:18:04.557 --> 00:18:07.527
The realms of men are always
noisy and irritating,

00:18:07.927 --> 00:18:10.096
but they seem to be doubly so today.

00:18:10.563 --> 00:18:11.698
Yase Douji!

00:18:11.898 --> 00:18:14.934
If everybody's out here
screwing around,

00:18:15.635 --> 00:18:18.938
Kurama Temple must not
have much work to do!

00:18:19.138 --> 00:18:20.473
On the contrary!

00:18:20.473 --> 00:18:24.711
What about you, Yase Douji?
Preparing for another tea party?

00:18:24.711 --> 00:18:27.413
It must be nice to have lots
of free time and lots of money,

00:18:27.413 --> 00:18:28.948
since you never leave the house.

00:18:37.056 --> 00:18:38.658
You! Bird!

00:18:38.891 --> 00:18:40.126
Bye, Yase Douiji!

00:18:41.027 --> 00:18:43.096
Hold it!

00:19:03.650 --> 00:19:05.952
Left at the next corner,
then directly to the right.

00:19:06.152 --> 00:19:06.786
All right!

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:37.050
Ushiwakamaru

00:19:39.519 --> 00:19:41.788
I-It's not mine.

00:19:44.524 --> 00:19:45.591
Darn it!

00:19:46.059 --> 00:19:52.565
Where did my controller go?!

00:20:01.374 --> 00:20:02.308
Yes, hello?

00:20:02.608 --> 00:20:04.177
Is this March Cafeteria?

00:20:04.777 --> 00:20:06.713
Yes. No, no, thank you.

00:20:07.647 --> 00:20:10.650
| actually had a question for you...

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:15.888
Bar Mackerel Street Cheers!

00:20:16.189 --> 00:20:19.559
Thank you, everybody! Nice work!

00:20:19.859 --> 00:20:21.561
Especially you, Fushimi! Great job!

00:20:21.561 --> 00:20:26.132
Today I learned that
| can really count on you!

00:20:31.838 --> 00:20:33.639
By the way, how did you...

00:20:38.478 --> 00:20:41.047
Eat Sleep Get Angry

00:20:41.914 --> 00:20:43.049
Bar
Mackerel Street

00:20:44.350 --> 00:20:46.719
Don't tell her. She'll get mad.

00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:51.424
Controller... Controller...
Let's party! Let's party!

00:20:53.626 --> 00:20:56.796
Installing that GPS was
a good idea, wasn't it?

00:21:00.767 --> 00:21:03.436
Before too long,
the Science Team will be going

00:21:03.436 --> 00:21:07.406
to the outside world with Kurama!

00:21:09.575 --> 00:21:11.010
| see three moons!

00:21:11.010 --> 00:21:11.978
Where are we?

00:21:11.978 --> 00:21:14.313
Is this the outside world?!

00:21:24.824 --> 00:21:27.193
Sounds like you caused
a lot of trouble today.

00:21:27.560 --> 00:21:29.328
Yes, I'm sorry.

00:21:29.729 --> 00:21:32.832
Shouko-san's antics were so amusing,
| let things get a bit out of hand.

00:21:32.832 --> 00:21:36.402
That controller was the first
thing she made when she came here.

00:21:36.402 --> 00:21:38.137
It's very important to her.

00:21:38.571 --> 00:21:39.772
Brings back memories.

00:21:39.772 --> 00:21:43.176
You're uncharacteristically
sentimental today.

00:21:44.243 --> 00:21:45.344
What about you?

00:21:45.578 --> 00:21:49.816
Has meeting someone from your place
of employment made you homesick?

00:21:53.920 --> 00:21:57.890
Those who work directly for
the High Priest are granted

00:21:57.890 --> 00:22:00.860
complete authority to act however
they please on a mission.

00:22:01.727 --> 00:22:03.229
So I was rather terrified.

00:22:03.963 --> 00:22:07.333
You're essentially a deserter, after all.

00:22:07.733 --> 00:22:09.101
Not at all.

00:22:09.402 --> 00:22:12.672
| seem to remember being
practically dragged here.

00:22:16.442 --> 00:22:18.744
And how goes the analysis
of this Aratama thing?

00:22:19.078 --> 00:22:20.146
It's going well.

00:22:20.713 --> 00:22:23.783
Whatever her other deficiencies,
the doctor is very talented.

00:22:26.519 --> 00:22:29.655
And the technology you brought
has contributed enormously.

00:22:31.257 --> 00:22:34.260
She says she'll help us, as well.

00:22:34.794 --> 00:22:36.762
| owe the Shrine a great deal.

00:22:38.598 --> 00:22:41.567
What about the possibility that
she's your parents' child?

00:22:41.868 --> 00:22:42.735
80%.

00:22:43.569 --> 00:22:44.270
Then...

00:22:45.504 --> 00:22:49.041
It felt kind of like talking to my father.

00:22:50.643 --> 00:22:52.111
Especially those eyes...

00:22:52.879 --> 00:22:54.847
Brings back so many memories.

00:22:58.517 --> 00:23:00.553
| owe them a good deal for my birth,

00:23:00.820 --> 00:23:03.122
but they need to come back.

00:23:04.123 --> 00:23:06.525
I'm tired of waiting.

00:23:08.294 --> 00:23:09.862
| want to leave this place.

00:23:10.396 --> 00:23:12.398
I'm tired of being a babysitter.

00:23:14.367 --> 00:23:15.968
It won't be long.

00:23:16.969 --> 00:23:20.439
It won't be long before
our wish comes true.

00:23:36.689 --> 00:23:38.157
| can't wait.

00:23:47.266 --> 00:23:53.673
I'd even cut things off, (Ouch!)
to prove the fact I exist.

00:23:55.508 --> 00:24:01.614
Though eternal lies surround me,
they're my safety line.

00:24:03.416 --> 00:24:10.022
"Wanna take you high?"
The galaxy shakes. You smile.

00:24:11.590 --> 00:24:18.064
I want to touch you. I don't want
to hear that it's forbidden.

00:24:19.865 --> 00:24:23.536
Moved to emotion by arguments,
| cast aside reason.

00:24:23.536 --> 00:24:28.641
I enter a game of risk that's
devoid of reason.

00:24:31.911 --> 00:24:36.682
It's resplendent with rare pain.

00:24:40.119 --> 00:24:45.191
Mistaking the real for the unreal.

00:24:48.327 --> 00:24:52.231
It transcends all understanding.

00:24:52.231 --> 00:24:53.165
So, fight!

00:24:56.435 --> 00:24:57.303
So, fight!

00:25:00.539 --> 00:25:01.374
So, fight!

00:25:08.581 --> 00:25:09.482
So, fight!

00:25:10.049 --> 00:25:12.018
K'Yy O U S O UG I G A

00:25:12.685 --> 00:25:15.755
There are some things you
can never give up, right?

00:25:16.322 --> 00:25:19.125
And I've got a lot of them!

00:25:19.492 --> 00:25:24.096
Precious treasures, filled with
memories of my mother...

00:25:25.097 --> 00:25:28.034
Treasures... my treasures...

00:25:28.868 --> 00:25:30.536
And you...

00:25:30.836 --> 00:25:34.840
| DTS B ST Next time: "The Second
Daughter and Her Wonderful Monsters."™

00:25:35.541 --> 00:25:38.144
Nothing can take the place of memories.
